sentences.l:
But you to the temple of Athena the spoil-driver
go, and I will go after Paris, that I may call him,
if he is willing to hear one speaking;

Of these one having lifted, Hecuba carried, a gift for Athena,
that which was fairest in its intricate work and largest,
and like a star it shone forth;

And when they came to the temple of Athena in the high city,
for them the doors opened Theano, fair-cheeked,
Cisseus’ daughter, wife of horse-taming Antenor;

while Hector to the house of Alexander had gone,
fine, which he himself built with men who then were the best
in rich-soiled Troy, builders,
